 ],
 "answer_text": "Found 1 gene record for BRCA1: BRCA1 DNA repair associated [2]. \n\nThe gene spans 22 exons across roughly 110 kb of DNA and forms the BRCA1-associated genome surveillance complex (BASC) together with other tumor suppressors and DNA damage sensors [1]. \n\nDNA Repair Function\n\nThe protein also associates with RNA polymerase II and interacts with histone deacetylase complexes, giving it a role in transcription and recombination [1]. \n\nCancer Significance\n\nMutations in BRCA1 are responsible for approximately 40% of inherited breast cancers and more than 80% of inherited breast and ovarian cancers [1]. \n\nGene records found\n\nGene NCBIGene:672, name: BRCA1 DNA repair associated [2]. Gene symbol: BRCA1 [3]. \n\nPubmed records found\n\nPubmed title: Mechanisms of Therapy Resistance in Patient-Derived Xenograft Models of BRCA1-Deficient Breast Cancer [4]. Pubmed title: BRCA1: An Endocrine and Metabolic Regulator [8]. Pubmed title: Preneoplastic stromal cells promote BRCA1-mediated breast tumorigenesis [11]. Pubmed title: Mechanism of BRCA1-BARD1 function in DNA end resection and DNA protection [14]. Pubmed title: Targeting GPX4-mediated ferroptosis protection sensitizes BRCA1-deficient cancer cells to PARP inhibitors [17]. \n\nClinvar records found\n\nClinvar title: NM_007294.4(BRCA1):c.5243_5277+2788del [5]. Clinvar title: NM_007294.4(BRCA1):c.5277+2916_5277+2946delinsGG [9]. Clinvar title: NG_005905.2:g.(147057_150288)_(160933_166866)del [12]. Clinvar title: GRCh37/hg19 17q21.31(chr17:41267743-41267796)x3 [15]. Clinvar title: NM_007294.4(BRCA1):c.2145C>G (p.Thr715=) [18]. \n\nOmim records found\n\nBRCA1 DNA REPAIR-ASSOCIATED PROTEIN [6]. BRCA1 [6]. \n\nClinical trial records found\n\nClinical trial name: Germline BRCA1 and BRCA2 Mutations in Jewish Women Affected by Breast Cancer [7]. Clinical trial name: BRCA1 Haploinsufficiency and Gene Expression [10]. Clinical trial name: Study to Evaluate Treatment Customized According to RAP80 and BRCA1 in Patients With Advanced Lung Carcinoma [13]. Clinical trial name: Letrozole in Preventing Breast Cancer in Postmenopausal Women With a BRCA1 or BRCA2 Mutation [16]. Clinical trial name: Recombinant Human Chorionic Gonadotropin in Preventing Breast Cancer in Premenopausal Women With BRCA1 Mutations [19]. "
